Dismiss suggestions on a retargeted touch outside the list.

A touch on the editor line immediately above the suggestion list can be
delivered with a suggestion row as its target. The gesture handler then
accepts that row even though the touch point lies outside the list.

Check the gesture's page coordinates against the list's page rectangle. If
they lie outside, run the editor's existing command to cancel suggestions
instead of accepting the row. The touch does not move the caret; a further
editor tap can do that. Mouse selection and touches within the list keep their
existing handling. Gesture dispatch and other lists are unchanged.

diff --git a/src/vs/editor/contrib/suggest/browser/suggestWidget.ts b/src/vs/editor/contrib/suggest/browser/suggestWidget.ts
